Permutation p < 0.05 (*): injecting the (weighted-sum) vector for ratio r reproduces real ratio-r ICL behavior better than chance relabeling. Bootstrap meanDiag/CI gives the effect size.
Note: with 10 ratios, adjacent ratios (e.g. 2-1-0 vs 1-2-0) are genuinely similar, so row-min/10 will be < 10 even when the effect is real — lean on the permutation p (pooled trace), which stays valid because random relabelings pair dissimilar ratios.
